WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.098
Smoke's going straight up this morning.
The thatch held through the night, then.

2
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.687
Held, aye. The wind off
the estuary tried it.

3
00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:18.458
This hill takes everything
the weather throws at it.

4
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:24.150
And gives it back. The children
slept warm round the fire.

5
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.379
That's all I asked of the night.

6
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.957
Look there, down the slope
to the north. Flat ground.

7
00:00:31.957 --> 00:00:35.736
Somebody will build on that
one day, mark my words.

8
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:41.719
Build what? There's nothing up here
but us, the cattle and the crows.

9
00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:44.699
No one has ever drawn
a line round this hill.

10
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:52.283
No line, no mark. We know where
it ends by the walking of it.

11
00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:57.586
Ask anyone in the valley whose hill
this is, they'll point at our smoke.

12
00:01:00.076 --> 00:01:04.176
Then let them point. One
house, one fire, one family.

13
00:01:04.176 --> 00:01:08.121
Anyone wants more of it
can come and argue with me.

14
00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.451
They'd lose. Fetch the little ones.

15
00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:16.361
We'll walk the edge before the
rain comes in over the water.

16
00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.634
Bore da. Yesterday we followed
a name across the hill.

17
00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.481
Today, something older than any name.

18
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:30.575
This is the Glamorgan-Gwent
Archaeological Trust report.

19
00:01:30.575 --> 00:01:40.849
They dug south of St Dochdwy's church and found what they call a possible
late Iron Age roundhouse, under a Roman villa of the second to fourth century.

20
00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:41.863
Published 1988.

21
00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.154
Mark the word 'possible'.

22
00:01:49.154 --> 00:01:53.347
The trench shows the outline of a
round building beneath the villa.

23
00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:58.352
It doesn't show who lived in it, what
they were called, or how long they stayed.

24
00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:07.042
And it doesn't tie anyone to the farm. No
deed, no family line reaches back that far.

25
00:02:07.042 --> 00:02:11.548
The dig itself gets its own
day, in 1979, where it belongs.

26
00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:22.186
For now, just the ground. A round house,
then stone laid over it. Tomorrow, the villa.
